 within and between two cultivars of red clover (<italic>Trifolium pratense </italic>L.)-Comparisons of morphological, isozyme, and RAPD markers</article-title><source>Euphytica</source><year>1995</year><volume>84</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>246</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Campos-De-Quiroz</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ortega-Klose</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic variability among elite red clover (<italic>Trifolium pratense </italic>L.) parents used in Chile as revealed by RAPD markers</article-title><source>Euphytica</source><year>2001</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>67</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>K&#x000f6;lliker</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Herrmann</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Boller</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Widmer</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Swiss Mattenklee landraces, a distinct and diverse genetic resource of red clover (<italic>Trifolium pratense </italic>L.)</article-title><source>Theor Appl Genet</source><year>2003</year><volume>107</volume><fpage>306</fpage><lpage>315</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12845445</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Herrmann</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Boller</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Widmer</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>K&#x000f6;lliker</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimization of bulked AFLP analysis and its application for exploring diversity of natural and cultivated populations of red clover</article-title><source>Genome</source><year>2005</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>474</fpage><lpage>486</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16121244</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dias</surname><given-names>PMB</given-names></name><name><surname>Julier</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Sampoux</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Barre</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Dall'Agnol</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic diversity in red clover (<italic>Trifolium pratense </italic>L.) revealed by morphological and microsatellite (SSR) markers</article-title><source>Euphytica</source><year>2007</year><volume>160</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>205</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cone</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>McMullen</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Bi</surname><given-names>IV</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Yim</surname><given-names>YS</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardiner</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Polacco</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanchez-Villeda</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fang</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Schroeder</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Havermann</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowers</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Paterson</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Soderlund</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Engler</surname><given-names>